# The Firebase Web API key. Public by design — it is already shipped inside the
# browser bundle and is greppable by anyone using the app. It is here because
# Identity Toolkit's REST endpoint is keyed, and functions/src/mcp.ts needs it to
# exchange a custom token for the ID token an MCP client sends back as a Bearer.
#
# Named PULSE_ rather than FIREBASE_ because `FIREBASE_` is a RESERVED prefix
# for function environment variables — using it makes the whole .env fail to
# load, taking every function with it, with only "Failed to load environment
# variables from .env" to go on.
#
# Not a secret, so not in Secret Manager: putting a public value there would
# imply a confidentiality it does not have, and add a rotation ritual for
# nothing.
PULSE_WEB_API_KEY=AIzaSyDaJb4cTE_c46qBSZ-4HhdV2srAiHN7KkU
